 :watchdog {:ownership "The independently reviewed watchdog is the external parent of a single opaque fixed controller process, outside the transient unit. It establishes and retains its own authenticated manager control transport, chooses a fresh unpredictable exact unit identity, and itself submits the fixed unit creation request. It never adopts a unit created by another actor; existing name, uncertain submission or missing invocation identity means fail closed. The controller may request only fixed admission operations over a private authenticated bounded protocol, never arbitrary units, argv or manager methods."
